00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:03.710 align:start position:0%
over the past decade we've seen a  drastic change in the types of traffic  patterns that application developers  have to plan for one day you could be at  standard traffic and the next needing to  scale to handle tens of thousands more  visitors this of course leads to all  sorts of issues with cost response times  and scale and there's no place in your  application where this is felt more than  in your database whether it's dealing  with scale or just struggling to fit  unstructured data into a relational  schema design most relational databases  struggle to solve these issues this is  where Couchbase comes in as a highly  scalable high-performance no SQL  document database Couchbase is one of  the fastest new SQL databases available  entirely designed with modern  applications in mind and right now  there's nothing more modern than running  a database using kubernetes see  kubernetes has rapidly increased in  sophistication with things like  operators persistent volumes helping  developers transition to the cloud and  scale where they need to this is why  we've built a special kubernetes  operator called the Couchbase autonomous  operator and it gives you the ability to  deploy multi node clusters by writing a  small configuration and pushing it to  kubernetes recovering automatically from  node failures automatically scaling your  cluster up or down as load from the  application changes ensuring that nodes  in the cluster are evenly split across  racks or zones in the data center  you can also automatically upgrade the  cluster to a newer version of Couchbase  server and manage cluster configuration  to ensure that the configuration is  properly set in your cluster and to help  bring this power to you without all the  headaches we've teamed up with the GCP  marketplace to make deploying and  managing Couchbase completely automated  let's take a quick look at how easy it  is to setup a cowfish cluster on gke  using the Couchbase autonomous operator  through the GCP marketplace the first  thing you need to do is log into GCP and  navigate to the google kubernetes engine  then click the applications link to get  to the applications marketplace click  deploy from the marketplace and then  scroll down to get to the Couchbase  autonomous operator click the configure  button to configure a new operator and  then make sure that the operator is  going to be installed into the correct  cluster in our case standard cluster 1  and click deploy it'll take a few  moments to actually deploy the operator  but once it's done you should get to  screen that looks like this this means  that the Couchbase operator has been  successfully deployed and that you can  now move forward to creating your first  Couchbase question the next thing that  you need to do is define a configuration  for your first Couchbase cluster that  you want to create in this example we  create a three node cluster with the  data index and query service one bucket  named default then we're running a  Couchbase enterprise 5.5 bit to push  this configuration to your kubernetes  cluster and the operator will  automatically start creating a new  cowfish cluster based on the  specification that we just defined after  a few minutes you should see that your  Couchbase cluster is created and you  have access to the Couchbase  administration console if you click on  the server's button you'll see that we  have a three node cluster created and if  you click on the buckets tab you'll see  that we have a default bucket just by  running a few commands we can use the  Couchbase operator to deploy the cluster  for us if any of our Couchbase notes  fail then the operator will get the  Couchbase cluster back into a healthy  state if we need to upgrade the cluster  to a later version in the future and we  can have the operator take care of the  upgrade for us  we aim to make management of Couchbase  clusters a thing of the past an envision  a world where users no longer need to  focus on managing their infrastructure  and can spend all their time building  their applications and when it comes to  running the Couchbase autonomous  operator on Google's gke  it just works visit the GCP marketplace  today to set up a Couchbase cluster on  gke or visit the link below to learn  more  [Music]
 

